      "content": "i know, i know. people always say there's beauty in the struggle or whatever. but it feels fake. it feels like watching a slow-motion wreck where you already know how it ends. if the end is guaranteed, and it's just going to be more pain and more loss, why is it considered \"better\" to just force yourself to sit through the middle part? shouldn't there be some dignity in just... letting go before it gets even uglier?",
